Did that and found only two cases which work for players benefit.

1. You can query your inventory while blind and not touch a footrice 
corpse that's in your inventory.

Do we actually want to change this?

2. If player character is levitating or flying a creature that tries to 
attack players legs is incapable to do it regardless if the attacker 
itself is flying or levitating.

But the only monster having AD_LEGS as its attack is xan and I don't 
know if they can fly or levitate.

All others seemed to either work against the player in a minor way or 
dealt with interface issues.

So that wasn't very good way to find misfeatures in the game. At least 
to find what devteam thinks are misfeatures.

Here is one feature that I think is a misfeature:

Player can name the four unique items even though she cannot name any 
artifacts (naming Sting or Orcrist is not naming an artifact, one names 
an ordinary item that becomes an artifact).

 From the implemation perspective the four unique items are not 
artifacts, but from a gaming perspective they seem to be already named 
items just like any other artifact.

It would be trivial change to disallow the naming of the four unique items.

